WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.659
Greetings, brave adventurers!

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:05.710
Seekers of knowledge, explorers of the great
unknown!

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.200
No doubt by now you have heard the stories
of the noble Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.710
gentleman explorer and naturalist, also known
as SCP-1867.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:20.050
His exploits are known far and wide, though
some question the validity of his tales, due

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.480
to the simple fact that he is a neon sea slug
and not a human man.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.480
Bah!

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.480
These are, of course, fools!

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.480
A gentleman never lies about his grand escapades!

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:33.469
We have even covered Lord Blackwood before,
in “A Sea Snail's Fantasy SCP-1867 - A Gentleman,”

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:37.760
but never before have we taken a look at such
a daring account of his work.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.019
Today we discuss a most curious hunting expedition,
one that brought our Lord Blackwood face to

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:49.140
face with the great beast, the hard-to-destroy
reptile, SCP-682 itself!

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.870
What will become of our hero?

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.679
What sights will he see on his journey?

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:55.120
Let us find out.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.120
Tally-ho!

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.829
On May 14, 1883, months after nearly losing
his life while climbing Mt.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.680
Everest, Lord Blackwood received a letter
at his London home.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.950
Upon opening it, he saw that it was a formal
invitation from one Colonel Joseph D’Enfante,

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.160
of the French Army.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:16.439
It invited him to participate in a hunt for
a monster known as The Tarasque, that threatened

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.549
the lives and security of the French people.

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:24.060
Anyone who was able to slay the creature would
receive a handsome award of five million pounds

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.090
for their trouble.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.930
Unable to resist a challenge, the chance to
face off against a creature he had never heard

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:34.890
of before, or the allure of such an impressive
prize, Lord Blackwood sent off an acceptance.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.729
So what was the Tarasque?

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:41.500
Lord Blackwood’s research turned up a fearsome
description: it was a massive scaly creature

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.899
with a hide that seemed impossible to pierce,
that breathed fire and killed everything in

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:47.680
its path without batting an eye.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.850
A worthy foe indeed.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:53.040
By the end of the day, Lord Blackwood had
received an address where he would attend

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.439
a briefing before the hunt would commence.

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:59.399
The meeting was held at a private room in
the city, in an exclusive club.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:05.390
There were three other would-be hunters there,
Mr. Roosevelt from America, Mr. Dukov, from

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.160
Russia, and Mr. Harris, from England.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.159
The Colonel greeted the men, and told them
what they were up against.

00:02:11.159 --> 00:02:16.470
A beast had lain waste to a French town, ripping
men, women, and children to shreds and resisting

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.810
every blow dealt against it by the army.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:23.870
So, the Colonel vowed to gather expert scientists
and hunters, for if they could not take down

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.180
the monster, it was likely that no one could.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.659
On May 20th, the party arrived in France to
begin the great adventure.

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:36.470
Each man brought his own armaments, a combination
of specialized weapons and knowledge, for

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.799
the task at hand.

00:02:37.799 --> 00:02:42.190
The following day, the Colonel escorted the
men to the quarantine zone, where the beast’s

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.190
attack had led it.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:47.470
Lord Blackwood was troubled by the sights
there, it was a city at war.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.090
Soldiers patrolled the streets, and barricades
were placed at the edge of town.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:55.640
Citizens were being evacuated as soldiers
aided them, and few had seen the beast themselves.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.700
At least, they had not been unfortunate enough
to see it up close.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.180
Beyond the quarantine barrier, it was hell
on earth.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.569
There were bodies laying in the streets, buildings
burnt to the ground, castles and stone walls

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:09.549
reduced to piles of rubble.

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:14.819
There was not one living thing in sight, not
a person, a farm animal, or even so much as

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:15.819
an insect.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:21.180
The men set up camp near the edge of the town,
and Mr. Harris set about tracking the beast.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.939
Before too long, he had found it, to the southwest,
and the next day they would set off after

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:26.939
it.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:31.160
The next day, the party made its way southwest
to Belleville, following a trail of destruction.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.819
There, they found it having a nap in the sun.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:38.800
It was longer than a whale, taller than a
giraffe, and bigger than both.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.810
Lord Blackwood thought that, if it had any
visible wings, he would consider it a dragon.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:47.360
They approached slowly, careful not to wake
the Tarasque.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.720
Lord Blackwood crouched behind a fence, steadied
his gun, and fired right at its head.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.630
The shot hit, and the top of the Tarasque’s
head came off with its impact.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:01.799
It seemed as if the beast was, after so much
pomp and circumstance, dead right there.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:04.410
But sadly, it was not.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:09.230
It sprang to life, blood and brains dripping
from its open skull as it turned to the men

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.269
and roared, then charged.

00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:15.930
The men scattered, firing their guns as they
ran, the monster gaining on them faster and

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:20.320
faster until Mr. Dukov fired into its open
wound with an electric rifle.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.400
It was stunned long enough for the men to
make it onto their horses.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.220
As they rode away, the monster continued to
chase them, new skin and bone growing over

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.060
what had once been a hole in its skull.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.960
Lord Blackwood fired a particle destabilizer
at its leg, tearing it off, but as he watched

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.810
in horror…the leg began to grow back.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.669
The hunting party managed to escape with their
lives, though their confidence was thoroughly

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:46.669
shaken.

00:04:46.669 --> 00:04:49.320
They rested that night with the soldiers at
the barricade.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.940
They attempted to attack the Tarasque again
the following day, but failed once more.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:59.970
The men realized that a simple gunshot, electrocution,
or fire would not be enough to kill the monster.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:04.300
It simply healed too fast, and its tolerance
for pain was too high.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.680
In order to kill it, they realized, they would
have to render it immobile and destroy its

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.419
body so thoroughly that it would die before
it could rebuild itself.

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:16.990
And so, they decided to set a trap.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:21.810
They dug a massive trench, wide and long enough
for the monster, and deep enough that it would

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.800
not be able to climb out before they had killed
it.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:30.289
In the bottom of the pit, they placed hundreds
of steel spikes, the tips dipped in poison.

00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:34.330
They placed a bridge across it, strong enough
for the men and horses but weak enough to

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.990
break under the Tarasque’s weight, and covered
it all with grass and leaves.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.840
Now, they just had to wait.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.440
Mr. Roosevelt acted as bait, approaching the
monster on horseback and attacking it with

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.860
a gunshot, then running and leading it back
toward the trap.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.000
As Roosevelt raced across the bridge, the
creature pursued him, and fell into the pit

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.990
where it was impaled on the spikes.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:58.880
Then, the men rained down hellfire.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.550
They shot it with bullets, explosives, jellied
kerosene.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:09.120
Mr. Dukov fired a pitchblende-gun that, upon
firing, released a blur of smoke and fire.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.990
Once the fire had receded, all that remained
was a skeleton.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:18.620
The men took the skull, charred from the flames,
and planned to take it back as a trophy.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.960
All was well!

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.400
Or so it seemed…

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.650
The men returned to the town with the monster’s
skull in tow, and the soldiers cheered at

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.650
the sight.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:31.450
They posed for photographs, and Mr. Dukov
decided to pose with his head between the

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.940
jaws of the beast.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:37.680
This was a grave mistake on his part, and
the jaws closed tight around his neck, his

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.389
head falling to the ground.

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:45.770
The skull acted on its own, rolling and biting,
all the while growing fresh skin and scales.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:55.500
It opened its gaping maw and shouted: “"Vous
me rendez malade.”

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.289
Screams rang out behind Lord Blackwood and
he turned to see…the rest of the Tarasque’s

00:07:00.289 --> 00:07:06.009
body, a headless corpse covered with stringy
bits of muscle and slowly growing brand new

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:07.009
flesh.

00:07:07.009 --> 00:07:11.289
It stomped through the field, crushing men
and tents beneath its great feet on its way

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:13.190
to reclaim its head.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:17.020
Mr. Harris ran for the bank vault, to grab
a weapon he had only referred to previously

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.599
as “his secret weapon.”

00:07:19.599 --> 00:07:24.210
Lord Blackwood chased after him, and found
Harris pulling a large crate, which he opened

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.830
with a sense of desperation.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:31.990
There, inside, was a sarcophagus, bound in
chains and covered in ancient runes.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:36.419
Blackwood begged Harris to leave the thing
behind and run for his life, but he did not

00:07:36.419 --> 00:07:41.360
have a chance to finish before Harris opened
the lid, and an arm wielding a sword emerged

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.910
and sliced his head from his body.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:49.210
A man emerged from the sarcophagus, naked,
wielding a sword, covered in tattoos.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:53.200
Blackwood had no way of knowing this, but
the man was none other than the deadly warrior

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.490
SCP-076, or Able.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.400
The mysterious man attacked Blackwood and
Roosevelt, and though they tried to defend

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.520
themselves, no weapon seemed to have an effect
on him.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:09.070
He was preparing to deliver a final blow to
Blackwood, and kill him once and for all,

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:12.620
when the Tarasque burst through the wall of
the building with a mighty bellow.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.570
At the sight of the enormous monster, Able
turned his focus from the two men to the beast.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:24.490
And so, the two seemingly unkillable creatures,
driven by bloodlust and inhuman strength,

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:26.060
began to fight.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.169
It took over an hour, and left destruction
and death in its wake.

00:08:30.169 --> 00:08:34.760
Able armed himself with explosives, mounting
them to his chest along with the pitchblende

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.500
gun, and ran toward the Tarasque.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:41.600
Knowing what would come next, Roosevelt and
Blackwood locked themselves in the bank vault,

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.130
and prayed that someone would find them before
they starved to death.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:50.110
After two days, the men were saved by a major
of the army, who was leading a group of soldiers

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.790
in a search for any survivors.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:56.060
They were taken to the hospital, and nursed
back to health by the staff there as well

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.589
as a friend of Blackwood’s named Henry.

00:08:58.589 --> 00:09:03.000
The major who rescued them told them that
Colonel was dead, and so were ten thousand

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.590
others claimed by the massive explosion.

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:11.010
The Tarasque and Able had both disappeared,
and there was no indication of where either

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.780
of them had gone.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:17.130
All that was left was destruction and the
memory that a true monster had made itself

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:19.170
known on French soil.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:24.170
Now, the only thing left to do was recover,
as best as anyone could.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:27.710
It would certainly take a very long time.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:32.610
The army was very suspicious of both Roosevelt
and Blackwood, as the only survivors of an

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.760
explosion so large it had been seen throughout
France.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:41.700
They demanded to know how the two had survived,
and what they had seen.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:46.980
Throughout this process, an Englishman watched
and took notes, but did not speak a word.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.750
Roosevelt and Blackwood were eventually released,
but they did not receive a penny of their

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:55.320
promised reward, and were told they could
not return to France again for the rest of

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.630
their lives.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:01.110
They were not to speak a word of what they
had seen to anyone, or there would be dire

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.110
consequences.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:07.290
In Calais, the two survivors said goodbye,
and Roosevelt announced he would return to

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.700
America to pursue a career in politics.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.730
Who can say what happened to him after that?

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:17.330
Upon returning to his home in London, Lord
Blackwood found that he had received a postcard.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:22.360
It read: “The Royal Foundation for the Security,
Containment, and Protection of Anomalous Objects

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:27.730
and Phantasmagoria requests a meeting for
the purpose of negotiating an alliance favourable

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.420
to both our parties.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:34.940
Please call any time (except Sundays) at No.
19 Marylebone Road, Westminster, and ask to

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.520
speak to Doctor Thursday.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.060
Your discretion is requested in this matter.”

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:42.070
He was puzzled by this note, unsure of what
to make of it.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.100
Perhaps, he thought, he could see what they
had to say.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:48.640
After all, he was always curious and ready
to explore new territory.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.700
Once he had recovered sufficiently, he would
reach out to this strange group and see what

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.780
they might have to offer him.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:11:00.510
And so began a new chapter of Lord Blackwood’s
story, one that included a mysterious organization

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.580
called The SCP Foundation.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:11.690
Now go check out “A Sea Snail's Fantasy
SCP-1867 - A Gentleman” and “SCP-682 - Ways

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:16.610
SCP Foundation Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy
Reptile” for more about the two anomalies

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.880
featured in today’s thrilling tale!

